          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പാട്ട് — pāṭṭŭ — a song."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് നല്ല പാട്ടാണ്. — itŭ nalla pāṭṭāṇŭ — \"This is a good song.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Listen to the join and you will hear nothing arrive. പാട്ട് (pāṭṭŭ) ends in the breathed half-u, and the chapter before last told you what those do when an ending comes: they step aside and let it land."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "word",
                "joined to ആണ്"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "word: നല്ലത്. joined to ആണ്: നല്ലതാണ് (nallathāṇŭ).",
                "word: പാട്ട് (pāṭṭŭ). joined to ആണ്: പാട്ടാണ് (pāṭṭāṇŭ)."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have done this before without a new word to do it on. നല്ലതാണ് has been in the book since the opinion chapter. പാട്ടാണ് is the same event on a word you met a moment ago — no യ, no വ, nothing inserted."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pāṭṭŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pāṭṭŭ*]"
            },
            {
