              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say a song. Then say to play."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പാടുക — pāṭuka — to sing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഞാൻ പാടുന്നു. — ñān pāṭunnu — \"I sing.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Last chapter the noun sat inside the verb. This pair is not built that way."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "noun",
                "verb"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "noun: കളി. verb: കളിക്കുക — the noun is there whole.",
                "noun: പാട്ട് (pāṭṭŭ). verb: പാടുക (pāṭuka) — the ട്ട thins to a single ട."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say them one after the other and you will hear it: പാട്ട് (pāṭṭŭ) holds the ṭ long, പാടുക (pāṭuka) does not."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words, one pattern between them — and that is all it is. Do not go looking for a doubled letter in every noun that sits beside a verb. These two are the pair this chapter gives you, and the book has not shown you a third."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pāṭuka",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pāṭuka*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ñān pāṭunnu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ñān pāṭunnu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pāṭṭŭ, then pāṭuka, and hear the long ṭ shorten",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pāṭṭŭ*, then *pāṭuka*, and hear the long **ṭ** shorten]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is to sing? (പാടുക (pāṭuka).) What is a song? (പാട്ട് (pāṭṭŭ).) What happens to the ട്ട in the verb? (It thins to a single ട.)"
            }
          ]
        }
