          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നൃത്തം — nṛtthaṁ — dance."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് നല്ല നൃത്തമാണ്. — itŭ nalla nṛtthamāṇŭ — \"This is a good dance.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is the third join, and the book has had it longest. നൃത്തം (nṛtthaṁ) ends in the ം, and you have known since the good-and-bad chapter what that sign does when ആണ് arrives: it is already the m, and it takes the full letter മ so it can carry the vowel behind it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "word ends in",
                "joined to ആണ്"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "word ends in: the half-u. joined to ആണ്: പാട്ടാണ് (pāṭṭāṇŭ).",
                "word ends in: ം. joined to ആണ്: നൃത്തമാണ് (nṛtthamāṇŭ)."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words, two different endings, and neither one gains a sound. The first gives one up; the second only changes how its m is written."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
