          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have a word that ends exactly as this one does. കഥ (katha)'s last letter is ഥ, carrying its own അ — and സിനിമ ends in അ too. So the same യ slides in:"
            },
            {
