        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: three endings, three different events",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four words met ആണ് in this chapter and the one before, and no two of the three endings did the same thing:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "word",
                "joined to ആണ്",
                "what happened"
              ],
              "columns": 3,
              "rowCount": 4,
              "utterances": [
                "word: പാട്ട് (pāṭṭŭ). joined to ആണ്: പാട്ടാണ് (pāṭṭāṇŭ). what happened: ends in the half-u — a sound is given up.",
                "word: നൃത്തം (nṛtthaṁ). joined to ആണ്: നൃത്തമാണ് (nṛtthamāṇŭ). what happened: ends in ം — the m is re-spelled.",
                "word: കഥ. joined to ആണ്: കഥയാണ് (kathayāṇŭ). what happened: ends in അ — a യ is added.",
                "word: സിനിമ. joined to ആണ്: സിനിമയാണ് (sinimayāṇŭ). what happened: ends in അ — a യ is added."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Given up, re-spelled, added — three different events, and the only thing that tells you which you are looking at is how the word ended."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പാട്ട് (pāṭṭŭ) is the song; പാടുക (pāṭuka) is doing it. Unlike കളി and കളിക്കുക, the noun is not sitting whole inside the verb — the long ṭṭ thins to a single ṭ:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഞാൻ പാടുന്നു. — ñān pāṭunnu — I sing."
            }
          ]
        },
